// The tailnet policy as the PA leaves it. The assistant's VM gave up its Tailscale identity in
// v0.13 (#91), and no PA VM is on the tailnet: the owner reaches them with `incus exec` on the
// devbox. Merge this into the tailnet policy file (admin console → Access controls); don't paste
// over it.
//
// - Delete everything that names tag:pa: its tagOwners entry, the grant from the owner's devices
//   to tag:pa, and the ssh rule into tag:pa as assistant.
// - Keep the grant below, so the owner's devices (user-owned, untagged) still reach each other,
//   the devbox included (the wiki's Obsidian view pulls over SSH on the tailnet).
// - Don't bring back a rule with "*" as its source, the default allow-all among them.
{
	"grants": [
		// The owner's devices reach each other. Tagged devices aren't anyone's own.
		{"src": ["autogroup:member"], "dst": ["autogroup:self"], "ip": ["*"]},
	],
}
